Adding syntactic support for recursive rows which can appear as result of type inference.

Modified syntax:
- [x] Effect rows can now be recursive
  Example:
  ```links
  fun w(g) {
    handle( g() ) {
      case Return(()) -> ()
      case F(h, res) -> w(h)
    }}
  ```
  has inferred type `(() { |(mu a . F:(() { |a}~> ()) {}-> _::Any|c)}~> ()) {F{_}|c}~> ()`, which can now be also entered. Note that I used the vertical bar, this seems consistent with how effect syntax usually is: `() { |a}~> ()`
  Closes #989 
- [x] Variants use separate production rules (involving uppercase and vbar) than the other row-based structures, so the recursive variables within them cannot mix.
  ```links
  links> sig f : ([|(mu a . Foo:()|Bar:()|d)|]) -> () fun f(_) { () };
  f = fun : ([||(mu a . Bar|Foo|_)|]) -> ()

  links> sig f : ([|(mu a . foo:()|bar:()|d)|]) -> () fun f(_) { () };
  ***: Parse error: <stdin>:1
  
    sig f : ([|(mu a . foo:()|bar:()|d)|]) -> () fun f(_) { () };
                           ^ 

  links> sig g : ((|(mu a. foo:()|bar:()|d))) -> () fun g(_) { () };
  ***: Parse error: <stdin>:1
  
    sig g : ((|(mu a. foo:()|bar:()|d))) -> () fun g(_) { () };
                                 ^ 

  links> sig g : ((|(mu a. foo:(),bar:()|d))) -> () fun g(_) { () };
  g = fun : ((|(mu a . bar,foo|_))) -> ()
  ```
  (Parse errors as expected here). Closes #990

Useful for implementing the following pattern in Pipeline jobs:

```groovy
import org.jenkinsci.plugins.workflow.steps.FlowInterruptedException

currentBuild.result = 'SUCCESS'

try {
  […] // Main
} catch (FlowInterruptedException fie) {
  currentBuild.result = fie.result.toString()
  throw fie
} catch (err) {
  currentBuild.result = 'FAILURE'
  throw err
} finally {
  […] // Something that needs access to the result, like sending a Slack message
}
```

I suggest that the example on the [the CloudBees support site](https://support.cloudbees.com/hc/en-us/articles/218554077-how-to-set-current-build-result-in-pipeline) be updated as described above. This version is better because it allows aborted builds to propagate their `ABORTED` status to the notification.

Adds `Matrix2D` class, which will eventually be how transforms + camera view culling will are controlled. This is a standard 3x3 Matrix implementation, but focused on use with the 2D context, with a transformation function that can be used directly with `HTMLRenderingContext2D.setTransform`:

```
const ctx = canvas.getContext("2d");
const m1 = Matrix2D.Identity.clone();
ctx.setTransform(...m1.toTransform());
```

